{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "03313",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 0.92,
      "end_seconds": 5.82,
      "duration_seconds": 4.9,
      "text": "Ready for you doctor. I'll stay in case you need anything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 6.51,
      "end_seconds": 10.78,
      "duration_seconds": 4.27,
      "text": "Thanks, that's helpful. Hello, please sit. What's been happening?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 11.84,
      "end_seconds": 20.02,
      "duration_seconds": 8.18,
      "text": "right, um, honestly, it's vomiting once or twice, and my family pushed me to come"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 21.81,
      "end_seconds": 24.1,
      "duration_seconds": 2.29,
      "text": "let's run through your medicines"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 25.64,
      "end_seconds": 37.96,
      "duration_seconds": 12.32,
      "text": "I mean, uh, I take something called vals... valsartan, 80 milligrams, maybe, once a day for my blood pressure"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 39.29,
      "end_seconds": 43.34,
      "duration_seconds": 4.05,
      "text": "do you have the packet or the prescription with you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 44.45,
      "end_seconds": 55.09,
      "duration_seconds": 10.64,
      "text": "Not with me. I'll bring it next time. It's, It's paracetamol, 650 milligrams, when needed for the knee pain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 55.57,
      "end_seconds": 56.5,
      "duration_seconds": 0.93,
      "text": "mm, okay"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 57.42,
      "end_seconds": 63.15,
      "duration_seconds": 5.73,
      "text": "I take oral rehydration solution, 1 sachet, after each loose stool"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 66.52,
      "end_seconds": 69.78,
      "duration_seconds": 3.26,
      "text": "How long has it been like this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 73.88,
      "end_seconds": 75.9,
      "duration_seconds": 2.02,
      "text": "probably five days. Yeah"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 77.14,
      "end_seconds": 85.67,
      "duration_seconds": 8.53,
      "text": "Alright, can you describe it a bit more for me? How strong it is, what the pattern is, what helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 87.64,
      "end_seconds": 94.09,
      "duration_seconds": 6.45,
      "text": "I'd say moderate honestly on and off. Sips of fluid helps a bit"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 96.02,
      "end_seconds": 99.44,
      "duration_seconds": 3.42,
      "text": "What about loose stools, have you noticed that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 100.41,
      "end_seconds": 104.21,
      "duration_seconds": 3.8,
      "text": "So, yeah. About a month, I'd say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 105.2,
      "end_seconds": 107.78,
      "duration_seconds": 2.58,
      "text": "How much does it limit you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 108.59,
      "end_seconds": 125.26,
      "duration_seconds": 16.67,
      "text": "Okay, so it feels severe to me. I've also had a mild tummy ache, for four weeks. I mean, as for mild tummy ache, it happens once or twice a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 126.59,
      "end_seconds": 132.4,
      "duration_seconds": 5.81,
      "text": "have you noticed blood in the stool no wet nappies or high fever?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 134.0,
      "end_seconds": 139.21,
      "duration_seconds": 5.21,
      "text": "okay, uh, so no, none that I've noticed"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 141.04,
      "end_seconds": 143.39,
      "duration_seconds": 2.35,
      "text": "did you notice any drowsiness?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 145.32,
      "end_seconds": 149.26,
      "duration_seconds": 3.94,
      "text": "hmm no I haven't had any drowsiness"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 150.57,
      "end_seconds": 155.76,
      "duration_seconds": 5.19,
      "text": "Have you noticed any weakness, or anything odd with your balance?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 157.33,
      "end_seconds": 159.41,
      "duration_seconds": 2.08,
      "text": "No, that's all normal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 160.76,
      "end_seconds": 164.96,
      "duration_seconds": 4.2,
      "text": "Let's talk a little about your daily life and habits."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 166.75,
      "end_seconds": 186.22,
      "duration_seconds": 19.47,
      "text": "I used to drink heavily but I stopped four years ago. No, I share a house with my brother. Not much, I mostly stay in these days. Lots of rice, lentils and some fruit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 187.83,
      "end_seconds": 192.33,
      "duration_seconds": 4.5,
      "text": "Has anything ever caused you a reaction? I mean any allergies."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 193.55,
      "end_seconds": 200.65,
      "duration_seconds": 7.1,
      "text": "Years back I got wheezing from diclofenac so I stay away from it now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 211.02,
      "end_seconds": 215.27,
      "duration_seconds": 4.25,
      "text": "Anything in your past medical history I should know?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 216.62,
      "end_seconds": 223.1,
      "duration_seconds": 6.48,
      "text": "I I have high blood pressure. I've had arthritis in my knees yes"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 225.02,
      "end_seconds": 234.25,
      "duration_seconds": 9.23,
      "text": "okay, so the vitals from earlier respiratory rate 15, BP is 114 over 73, oxygen saturation is 99 percent, heart rate 69."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 235.75,
      "end_seconds": 237.11,
      "duration_seconds": 1.36,
      "text": "Good, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 239.43,
      "end_seconds": 243.84,
      "duration_seconds": 4.41,
      "text": "I'd like to check you over now, if that's alright"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 245.3,
      "end_seconds": 246.31,
      "duration_seconds": 1.01,
      "text": "Sure thing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 248.18,
      "end_seconds": 249.62,
      "duration_seconds": 1.44,
      "text": "Look straight ahead."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 266.64,
      "end_seconds": 271.23,
      "duration_seconds": 4.59,
      "text": "He is alert, drinking, with moist lips and a soft tummy."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 274.87,
      "end_seconds": 276.61,
      "duration_seconds": 1.74,
      "text": "you can relax now"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 288.85,
      "end_seconds": 303.36,
      "duration_seconds": 14.51,
      "text": "from what you've told me and what I found, it fits best with a mild stomach bug the reason I say that is that your story and my examination fit together"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 312.73,
      "end_seconds": 330.35,
      "duration_seconds": 17.62,
      "text": "and please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose. For now, no new medicines or tests are needed. Anything else on your mind before you go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 330.93,
      "end_seconds": 334.95,
      "duration_seconds": 4.02,
      "text": "Mm, uh, alright, thanks, take care."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 336.5,
      "end_seconds": 338.23,
      "duration_seconds": 1.73,
      "text": "So look after yourself."
    }
  ]
}